---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Spidergraph — Stack Builder"
  description="Pick a target tier, select what you actually run across 15 product slots, and see live gap analysis and a radar chart of your security coverage."
  path="privacy-stack-builder/"
  current="stack-builder"
  accent="teal"
>
  <link
    slot="head"
    rel="stylesheet"
    href={`${base}pages/privacy-stack-builder.css`}
  />

  <div class="wrap">
    <header>
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Configurator · 15 slots</div>
        <h1>
          Stack <span>Builder</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="sub">
          Pick what you currently run in each slot. The build compares it
          against the recommended part for your target tier and flags gaps —
          same idea as a hardware parts list, applied to a security stack.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-select">
        <div class="tier-label">Target build tier</div>
        <div
          class="tier-btns"
          id="tierBtns"
          role="group"
          aria-label="Target build tier"
        >
          <button
            type="button"
            class="tier-btn"
            data-tier="1"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            Budget
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="tier-btn active"
            data-tier="2"
            aria-pressed="true"
          >
            Mid
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="tier-btn"
            data-tier="3"
            aria-pressed="false"
          >
            No-Limit
          </button>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="reset-btn" id="resetBtn">
          Reset build
        </button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="platform-bar" id="platformBar">
      <div class="platform-field">
        <div class="tier-label">Desktop platform</div>
        <select id="platformDesktop">
          <option value="windows">Windows</option>
          <option value="macos">macOS</option>
          <option value="linux">Linux</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="platform-field">
        <div class="tier-label">Mobile platform</div>
        <select id="platformMobile">
          <option value="ios">iOS</option>
          <option value="android">Android</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="platform-hint" id="platformHint">
        Guessed from your browser — change either if wrong. Affects the two OS
        Hardening slots below.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rows-toolbar">
      <select id="sectionJump" class="section-jump" aria-label="Jump to domain">
        <option value="">Jump to domain…</option>
      </select>
    </div>

    <div class="layout">
      <div id="rows"></div>

      <div class="sidebar">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Coverage readout</div>
          <svg
            id="radar"
            width="280"
            height="280"
            viewBox="0 0 280 280"
            aria-hidden="true"
          ></svg>
          <div class="score-row">
            <div>
              <div class="score-num" id="scoreNum">
                0%
              </div>
              <div class="score-label">of target tier filled</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Build summary</div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Slots at target</span>
            <span class="v teal" id="mAtTarget">
              0/15
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Slots below target</span>
            <span class="v amber" id="mBelow">
              0
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Critical gaps (none set)</span>
            <span class="v red" id="mGap">
              0
            </span>
          </div>
          <div class="metric">
            <span class="k">Est. recurring cost / yr</span>
            <span class="v" id="mCost">
              $0
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Priority fixes</div>
          <div id="gapList" class="gap-list"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">Export</div>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="tier-btn active"
            id="reportBtn"
            style="display:block; width:100%; text-align:center; padding:11px; cursor:pointer;"
          >
            Generate report ↓
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card-title">History</div>
          <p class="small">
            Save a dated checkpoint to compare your build against past versions
            of itself.
          </p>
          <button
            type="button"
            id="snapshotBtn"
            class="reset-btn"
            style="width:100%; margin-bottom:12px;"
          >
            Save snapshot
          </button>
          <div id="historyList" class="history-list"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <footer>
      <b>Not in this picker:</b> social engineering discipline, physical
      security habits, and legal/documentation steps aren't product slots —
      they're behavior, not purchases. The companion <b>OPSEC Field Manual</b>{' '}
      covers exactly that discipline layer as a checklist; see{' '}
      <b>personal-security-playbook.md</b> for the full write-ups on those
      domains and the incident-response runbooks. Costs shown are rough annual
      estimates for the paid tier of each option and may not reflect current
      pricing — verify at checkout.
      <br />
      <br />
      <b>On the Linux/GrapheneOS recommendations:</b> Privacy Guides and
      Techlore rate Linux (desktop) and GrapheneOS (Android) as the stronger
      privacy default because mainstream proprietary OSes ship with telemetry
      that's genuinely hard to fully remove — see Privacy Guides'{' '}
      <a
        href="https://www.privacyguides.org/en/os/linux-overview/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        Linux Overview
      </a>{' '}
      and{' '}
      <a
        href="https://www.privacyguides.org/en/os/windows/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        Windows Overview
      </a>
      . Neither source treats staying on Windows, macOS, or iOS as a mistake —
      see Techlore's{' '}
      <a
        href="https://techlore.tech/the-real-privacy-enemy-is-ourselves/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener"
      >
        "The Real Privacy Enemy is Ourselves"
      </a>{' '}
      on shaming beginners and people who make informed, practical platform
      choices. Every platform above gets a real hardening ceiling either way.
      <br />
      <br />
      <b>On the ✓ verified / Legacy tags:</b> this isn't a static list — slots
      get re-checked against current vendor pricing and source guidance on the
      project's quarterly cycle (see <b>SOURCES</b> in a generated report). A{' '}
      <span class="verified-tag" style="margin-left:0;">
        ✓ verified
      </span>{' '}
      tag shows the date a slot's figures were last confirmed current; a slot
      with no tag hasn't been re-checked recently. When a figure changes, the
      old value isn't silently deleted — it's kept as a <b>Legacy</b> note
      directly under the current recommendation, so you can see what changed and
      when.
      <br />
      <br />
      Your build stays in this browser only, in <code>localStorage</code> —
      nothing is sent anywhere, so it's still here next time you come back for
      the quarterly re-audit the Playbook recommends. <b>Reset build</b> clears
      it.
    </footer>
  </div>

  <button
    type="button"
    id="scrollTopBtn"
    class="scroll-top-btn"
    aria-label="Scroll to top"
  >
    ↑
  </button>

  <script src={`${base}shared/persist.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}shared/history.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}shared/stack-builder-scoring.js`} is:inline></script>
  <script src={`${base}pages/privacy-stack-builder.js`} is:inline></script>
</BaseLayout>
